# examples/regressions/sys_mmap — the §16 FIFTH-CRUMB fixture (arena-over-mmap keystone
# sub-crumb A, `docs/design/plano-s16-arena-mmap.md` §7.1): proves the `syscall6`/`syscall2`
# codegen intrinsics issue the raw x86_64 Linux `mmap`/`munmap` syscalls that will back the §16
# arena's page allocator. A SELF-CONTAINED project (its own local copy of the `SYS_MMAP`/
# `SYS_MUNMAP`/`PROT_*`/`MAP_*` consts under `src/sys/sys.tks`), because the real `teko::sys`
# lives in the COMPILER's own project (root `teko`, reserved — no user project may claim it) and
# an external standalone project has no visibility into it — the `sys_write`/`sys_getrandom`
# precedent. The local copy is a byte-for-byte structural mirror of the consts `src/sys/sys.tks`
# actually uses, so building and running it exercises the identical `#os`/`#arch` prune mechanism
# the real module relies on.
name = "sys_mmap"
source = "src"

[artifact]
kind = "binary"
